Package: Ipse
Type: Package
Title: Layered Cell Type Annotation for Single-Cell and Spatial Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Harrison", , , "harrisonnott.au@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Assigns cell type labels to single-cell or spatial
    transcriptomic data from a marker gene reference bundled inside the
    package, with no external atlas or reference download required.
    Markers are layered so that lineage identity, functional programme,
    and condition-associated state are scored separately: labels are
    assigned from identity markers alone, so an annotation can never
    encode disease status, and a cell that retains its lineage while
    losing its effector programme is described rather than mislabelled.
    Condition signatures are opt-in, named, and carry their source.
    Includes tools for deriving markers from annotated reference data.
    Ships a midbrain reference; further regions are planned.
